#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063968 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064330 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0d0fdb7-9849-5aca-b494-3b013b2eb035" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Square Root of a Perfect Square Containing a Fraction"}] :question/id #uuid "62a47fad-0c27-5e6d-a21f-8b298ac11159" :question/math-academy-id "e-1355" :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt{\\dfrac{4x^2}{y^2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the square root of a perfect square can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{x^2} = |x|\n$$\n\nAlso, we notice that $4, x^2,$ and $y^2$ are all perfect squares.\n\nFirst, we write the expression under the square root as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{2}^{2}{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2\\cdot 2\\cdot x\\cdot x}{y\\cdot y}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2\\cdot x\\cdot 2\\cdot x}{y\\cdot y}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2x}{y}\\cdot \\frac{2x}{y}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{2x}{y})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the absolute value of the squared quantity and simplify using the rules of absolute value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{2x}{y})}^{2}} & =|\\frac{2x}{y}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|2x|}{|y|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2|\\cdot |x|}{|y|} \\\\  & =\\frac{2|x|}{|y|}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064122 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064279 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bb1eda0-9577-59e7-9c6c-b85966fbb7e4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Square Root of a Perfect Square Using Absolute Value"}] :question/id #uuid "d71c8752-131c-5c82-b642-dee1d03484f4" :question/math-academy-id "e-6737" :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt{16y^2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the square root of a perfect square can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{x^2} = |x|\n$$\n\nAlso, we notice that $16$ and $y^2$ are both perfect squares.\n\nFirst, we write the expression under the square root as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{16{y}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}\\cdot {y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 4\\cdot y\\cdot y} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot y\\cdot 4\\cdot y} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4y\\cdot 4y} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the absolute value of the squared quantity and simplify using the rules of absolute value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(4y)^{2}} & =|4y| \\\\  & =|4|\\cdot |y| \\\\  & =4|y|\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064141 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064305 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4a48a060-871e-5c31-b1c0-7c4ed10eb259" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying the Square Root of a Perfect Square With Multiple Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "6bf774f8-aaa7-5a8e-9fb5-1ed1356b87ae" :question/math-academy-id "e-9639" :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt{36a^2c^2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the square root of a perfect square can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{x^2} = |x|\n$$\n\nAlso, we notice that $36, a^2,$ and $c^2$ are perfect squares.\n\nFirst, we write the expression under the square root as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{36{a}^{2}{c}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}\\cdot {a}^{2}\\cdot {c}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6\\cdot 6\\cdot a\\cdot a\\cdot c\\cdot c} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6\\cdot a\\cdot c\\cdot 6\\cdot a\\cdot c} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(6ac)\\cdot (6ac)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(6ac)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the absolute value of the squared quantity and simplify using the rules of absolute value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(6ac)^{2}} & =|6ac| \\\\  & =|6|\\cdot |ac| \\\\  & =6|ac|\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064494 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064330 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0d0fdb7-9849-5aca-b494-3b013b2eb035" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Square Root of a Perfect Square Containing a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb0d9b8c-6095-5d0b-99f7-208fc4411b8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{p}{9q}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061196} {:answer/id #uuid "1b81a56c-810f-573a-97dd-301514efe747" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9|p|}{q}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481592} {:answer/id #uuid "9b93bd3e-5333-5ae7-b2a4-a70e11e54551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{p}{9q}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481615} {:answer/id #uuid "a58d28b3-647f-5745-b92e-54ec7959c4b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|p|}{9|q|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481618} {:answer/id #uuid "eade159a-6f25-56c3-9356-c512910ef15e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9p}{|q|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a58d28b3-647f-5745-b92e-54ec7959c4b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|p|}{9|q|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481618} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa61df20-116f-58fd-ad91-75f98fec1c35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dae30c03-3248-5393-af33-6d1d5e3a7a98" :question/math-academy-id "q-129392" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{\\frac{{p}^{2}}{81{q}^{2}}}=$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the square root of a perfect square can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nAlso, we notice that ${p}^{2},81,$ and ${q}^{2}$ are all perfect squares.\n\nFirst, we write the expression under the square root as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{{p}^{2}}{81{q}^{2}}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{p}^{2}}{{9}^{2}\\cdot {q}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{p\\cdot p}{9\\cdot 9\\cdot q\\cdot q}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{p\\cdot p}{9\\cdot q\\cdot 9\\cdot q}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{p}{9q}\\cdot \\frac{p}{9q}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{p}{9q})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the absolute value of the squared quantity and simplify using the rules of absolute value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{p}{9q})}^{2}} & =|\\frac{p}{9q}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|p|}{|9q|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|p|}{|9|\\cdot |q|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|p|}{9|q|}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481671 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064279 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bb1eda0-9577-59e7-9c6c-b85966fbb7e4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Square Root of a Perfect Square Using Absolute Value"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e891d34-6c44-5f95-b17b-99dd8094812d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481583} {:answer/id #uuid "12197615-b745-5519-9cc6-05632d3bf3bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481586} {:answer/id #uuid "b3e87eba-1191-550d-93b0-4de6bc1bc641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|z|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481622} {:answer/id #uuid "ee296152-fc8a-54a9-9d6f-71bbfd30d366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481645} {:answer/id #uuid "fef3c8c3-5a09-538a-8384-95b8300e46c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3e87eba-1191-550d-93b0-4de6bc1bc641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|z|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481622} :answer-field/id #uuid "afffccf8-b1b8-53bd-9ab1-fc9b40dfecf3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b1106a2d-af4e-5322-aea1-c8e92fa92e1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-129414" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{{z}^{2}}=$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the square root of a perfect square can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{z}^{2}}=|z|.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064305 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4a48a060-871e-5c31-b1c0-7c4ed10eb259" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying the Square Root of a Perfect Square With Multiple Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e16dc08-5030-54fb-9306-dca7223216e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm mn" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481582} {:answer/id #uuid "18258e03-ce58-5794-b33f-b39ccd74a623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "m|n|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481591} {:answer/id #uuid "325538a2-892e-5f60-99c8-26f9fc7cff4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|m|n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481594} {:answer/id #uuid "b57b45d6-4e0f-54be-a110-5581114af9e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "mn" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481623} {:answer/id #uuid "bcaad1fc-0e23-5f14-a129-448803e83d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|mn|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bcaad1fc-0e23-5f14-a129-448803e83d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|mn|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481629} :answer-field/id #uuid "379b678b-8a0f-54f4-be29-83e54dc529f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481654}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7244134b-92da-5194-8740-fd44c3d9b173" :question/math-academy-id "q-129430" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{{m}^{2}{n}^{2}}=$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the square root of a perfect square can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nAlso, we notice that ${m}^{2}$ and ${n}^{2}$ are perfect squares.\n\nFirst, we write the expression under the square root as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{m}^{2}{n}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{m\\cdot m\\cdot n\\cdot n} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{m\\cdot n\\cdot m\\cdot n} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(mn)\\cdot (mn)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(mn)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the absolute value of the squared quantity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(mn)^{2}} & =|mn|\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481673 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064305 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4a48a060-871e-5c31-b1c0-7c4ed10eb259" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying the Square Root of a Perfect Square With Multiple Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61381c90-de08-5a13-a098-eb1c4e1bf2de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{h}^{2}{k}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481605} {:answer/id #uuid "722cfa04-487a-530b-acba-80c4f56e5c8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7hk}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481609} {:answer/id #uuid "a3e1d779-fc09-5b5c-b902-bb741b10459b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7hk" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481617} {:answer/id #uuid "c611a85e-5714-52e9-b3f1-8a6f851d8b55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm 7hk" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481631} {:answer/id #uuid "d878ba9d-e27a-5610-a312-39fe41c2686c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7|hk|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d878ba9d-e27a-5610-a312-39fe41c2686c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7|hk|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481633} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b969c33-fde1-5cdb-94d7-ebf310e61844" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481657}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fbd7fbcf-f71d-5f1d-91fa-fd513daaf842" :question/math-academy-id "q-129440" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{49{h}^{2}{k}^{2}}=$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the square root of a perfect square can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nAlso, we notice that $49,{h}^{2},$ and ${k}^{2}$ are perfect squares.\n\nFirst, we write the expression under the square root as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{49{h}^{2}{k}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{{7}^{2}\\cdot {h}^{2}\\cdot {k}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{7\\cdot 7\\cdot h\\cdot h\\cdot k\\cdot k} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{7\\cdot h\\cdot k\\cdot 7\\cdot h\\cdot k} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(7hk)\\cdot (7hk)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(7hk)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the absolute value of the squared quantity and simplify using the rules of absolute value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(7hk)^{2}} & =|7hk| \\\\  & =|7|\\cdot |hk| \\\\  & =7|hk|\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481663 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064330 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0d0fdb7-9849-5aca-b494-3b013b2eb035" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Square Root of a Perfect Square Containing a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17341934-1f7c-517d-8c9b-00c031b8823a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{r}^{2}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481590} {:answer/id #uuid "40b07501-069c-515d-b0e4-25b6aea2080b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|r|}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481600} {:answer/id #uuid "684728cb-9a8a-5e94-9dd1-04eb633a68d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{r}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481606} {:answer/id #uuid "7ab85dd4-a67f-5d96-9874-b5311a0fcf49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|r|}{100}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481611} {:answer/id #uuid "e281c12c-09da-5127-85cb-7d8cc84bf743" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{r}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40b07501-069c-515d-b0e4-25b6aea2080b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|r|}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481600} :answer-field/id #uuid "903290b8-9d04-50ab-9ab9-3b30be15c773" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481658}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1ea1bc4b-df65-5c2e-8a1e-25b530d6cd97" :question/math-academy-id "q-129465" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{\\frac{{r}^{2}}{100}}=$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the square root of a perfect square can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nAlso, we notice that ${r}^{2}$ and $100$ are both perfect squares.\n\nFirst, we write the expression under the square root as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{{r}^{2}}{100}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{r}^{2}}{{10}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{r\\cdot r}{10\\cdot 10}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{r}{10}\\cdot \\frac{r}{10}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{r}{10})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the absolute value of the squared quantity and simplify using the rules of absolute value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{r}{10})}^{2}} & =|\\frac{r}{10}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|r|}{|10|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|r|}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233381 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064330 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0d0fdb7-9849-5aca-b494-3b013b2eb035" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Square Root of a Perfect Square Containing a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10e0df1d-e35f-5855-a834-1c94f1908569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{z}{5y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481585} {:answer/id #uuid "7c3d666f-f045-5443-9c6d-274e5c6211c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|z|}{5y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481612} {:answer/id #uuid "b1faed5d-4a27-57fd-9b17-4d064369014c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{z}{5y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481621} {:answer/id #uuid "dbac0fc6-9501-50df-88fb-33580ce66e8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{z}^{2}}{5{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481635} {:answer/id #uuid "e35cb55d-2dfd-55eb-bf0f-6fa62c65efa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|z|}{5|y|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e35cb55d-2dfd-55eb-bf0f-6fa62c65efa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|z|}{5|y|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481639} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6c4f3e7-b119-592e-9f35-31368c3f7121" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481660}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "97082509-6da1-5d7c-a3a4-921738c6eb05" :question/math-academy-id "q-129471" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25{y}^{2}}}=$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the square root of a perfect square can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nAlso, we notice that ${z}^{2},25,$ and ${y}^{2}$ are all perfect squares.\n\nFirst, we write the expression under the square root as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25{y}^{2}}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{5}^{2}\\cdot {y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{z\\cdot z}{5\\cdot 5\\cdot y\\cdot y}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{z\\cdot z}{5\\cdot y\\cdot 5\\cdot y}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{z}{5y}\\cdot \\frac{z}{5y}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{z}{5y})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the absolute value of the squared quantity and simplify using the rules of absolute value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{z}{5y})}^{2}} & =|\\frac{z}{5y}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|z|}{|5y|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|z|}{|5|\\cdot |y|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|z|}{5|y|}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064700 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064279 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bb1eda0-9577-59e7-9c6c-b85966fbb7e4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Square Root of a Perfect Square Using Absolute Value"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6059811-b154-518c-bedf-4cc3e1ea097f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062260} {:answer/id #uuid "6c5ced3c-b876-5f42-990a-d0b274158a72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062262} {:answer/id #uuid "9cf8f853-47b0-546f-aa83-1138277cd2d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3|a|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481616} {:answer/id #uuid "e65bbee3-f23e-5270-8ed5-1bab0dfe407b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3|a|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481641} {:answer/id #uuid "ed896dea-642f-5d08-9aad-65fc2c64b390" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm 3a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cf8f853-47b0-546f-aa83-1138277cd2d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3|a|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481616} :answer-field/id #uuid "84560ccf-15d0-5ae1-a76b-e2226fb8d257" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062257}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "18f5174a-b7a3-5d30-9f8e-6e4e9431c761" :question/math-academy-id "q-2873" :question/problem "$\\sqrt{9{a}^{2}}=$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the square root of a perfect square can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nAlso, we notice that $9$ and ${a}^{2}$ are both perfect squares.\n\nFirst, we write the expression under the square root as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{9{a}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}\\cdot {a}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3\\cdot 3\\cdot a\\cdot a} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3\\cdot a\\cdot 3\\cdot a} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3a\\cdot 3a} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3a)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the absolute value of the squared quantity and simplify using the rules of absolute value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(3a)^{2}} & =|3a| \\\\  & =|3|\\cdot |a| \\\\  & =3|a|\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
